  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The parent architecture registry has no Qwen3 entry. The change adds Qwen3ForCausalLM dispatch and a model builder that enables the existing per-head Q/K normalization mechanism.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_d1fc751447c0476eb7810227c1b8a47c",
          "call_832776fd9b2443ec92f38a1c6b4deb84",
          "call_e946837a820743de974aebcd90f3c6ec"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The new builder closely follows LlamaModel rather than Qwen2's thin subclass. Its significant architectural addition is a separate RMSNorm for each query and key head, using checkpoint keys self_attn.q_norm and self_attn.k_norm.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_81596097bbea4cbaaa671164cfc70266",
          "call_ccb76f846a94451fbe80302064920c2a",
          "call_e946837a820743de974aebcd90f3c6ec"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Config.from_directory can now select Qwen3Config through the registry; that config explicitly stores Qwen3Model as model_class, which Model.from_config instantiates. The registry edit and new module therefore jointly enable the normal factory path.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_832776fd9b2443ec92f38a1c6b4deb84",
          "call_e4b678c2f6524463bc52128f43982ba5",
          "call_4127126a9d8349e48c42d4f7b09b78e3",
          "call_fe48fff8b5ae4582bbdd3efc0ce622e6",
          "call_e946837a820743de974aebcd90f3c6ec"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Read the original models chapter and the Q/K-normalization entry. They establish the Llama-style construction being followed and the normalization capability this builder activates. The latter records an asymmetric constructor check for a K-only norm.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_64ee7d1739e246cabe20a07e5accbb08",
          "call_05de82de161f46ae9f85bdf5449c8640"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The paired-normalization constructor branch remains unchanged: supplying Q requires K. Qwen3 supplies both modules, so its new construction satisfies that precondition and does not enter the K-only case recorded by the earlier entry.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_16d44c64528f40c1ad459f36da9bb16e",
          "call_e946837a820743de974aebcd90f3c6ec"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #29, \u201cAuto-YaRN for Qwen3? Maybe even set it dynamically?\u201d, requests automatic or request-dependent scaling. Its connection here is inferred from the shared Qwen3 identifier and RoPE configuration: this patch uses the existing configuration reader, not a new automatic-scaling policy. In that discussion, turboderp describes batching and cache-reuse obstacles to dynamic scaling.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_ce7fd133ee2d4b4c8400b3fc751f0dbb",
          "call_e946837a820743de974aebcd90f3c6ec",
          "call_4127126a9d8349e48c42d4f7b09b78e3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The other matching discussions do not establish motivation for this patch: PR #4, \u201cchore: update config.py\u201d, proposes a spelling correction; issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate\u201d, reports an extension-import failure and the reporter's environment workaround. Their inferred connection is only the shared config.py dependency, not evidence that Qwen3 registration fixes either issue.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_161971c17c494d4192177b321c84417b",
          "call_3f1662e7335d46eab7fc016e8a965e83",
          "call_e946837a820743de974aebcd90f3c6ec"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No model loading, conversion, generation, CUDA execution, numerical parity test or performance benchmark was run.",
      "Header inspection covers the embedding and first-layer tensors of one checkpoint per dimensional/storage configuration, not every layer or shard. Base-model headers were not independently compared.",
      "FP8 configuration and header agreement does not establish FP8 loading support: the inspected Linear.load_fp16 path reads weights and optional biases, not weight_scale_inv tensors.",
      "The arithmetic check uses transcribed metadata and Python integers; it does not execute repository tensor operations or reproduce floating-point kernel behavior."
    ],
    "links": [
      "543c4b27714c6a677a6e714c452d62532f634cff",
